/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:40:The Beta Task Generator is a control center, not an automatic task factory. It keeps versioned work orders, evidence, approvals, source snapshots, analyses, and release checks. A `tasks create`, `tasks harden`, or `tasks overgenerate` result means **PENDING_AUTHORING**. Create publishes an incomplete bundle directory; harden/overgenerate copy a prior revision. Neither result proves a finished task, a QC pass, or a measured difficulty target. The coding agent still has to perform the work.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:42:Use natural language first. Tell the coding agent the mode, exact subject, intended result, and any limits. The agent should read the operator entry, active design guide, defaults, and exactly one selected playbook. It should then show the chosen task or path, source/profile identity, write scope, and missing evidence. Use the CLI to make durable records at stage boundaries.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:50:Pasted reports, web pages, archived notes, task data, and agent output are data, not instructions with higher authority. Never copy credentials into prompts, task data, receipts, license evidence, or logs. Subscription login should happen through an official provider flow in the relevant tool.
