/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:645:Every dependency key and value must be a known Q ID. Closure may not silently add a finding; the user must select it. Findings assessed as likely easier, likely harder, or unknown require an explicit risk choice: `fix alone`, `harden separately`, or `leave unresolved`. For expected-unchanged findings the controller does not always require a choice, though stating it can make your intent clearer. `leave unresolved` removes edit permission. `harden separately` needs explicit paths already listed in that finding's analyzed `dependent_files`; broader paths require new analysis and selection. Hardening paths shared with an excluded finding are blocked. `must_update_paths` must appear in the real diff; other allowed paths are conditional review scope.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:681:Inspect at any time with `python -B -m core qc-repair status CASE` or `python -B -m core qc-repair resume CASE`. If a case pauses or retains findings, use `qc-repair continue CASE --route selection` or `--route analysis`. Missing and failed checks do not resolve findings or reset counters. Three unsuccessful attempts pause before a fourth automatic edit. False-positive-only selection can finish by evidence rebuttal without a useless revision. Excluded Real findings yield `COMPLETE_WITH_FINDINGS`. Without comparable real runs, the report states harness-score impact is unmeasured and preserves old scores and trajectories as historical.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:691:Use the strongest reasoning model actually available in the account picker for task contracts, oracle/verifier disagreement, coupled rule analysis, QC triage, hardening decisions, and independent review. A faster model is suitable for low-risk formatting, inventory classification, or converting an already approved structure to JSON. For an important decision, obtain a fresh independent review. It may use the same model in a clean context or a different provider. Beta benchmark evidence does not prove a universal model ranking, so do not claim that one brand is always best.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:698:| Author or harden task files locally | Claude Code signed into Claude Pro; choose its strongest available suitable model | Supported subscription route with local tools; actual model access is account-specific |
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:703:| Measure whether your task defeats the target | The configured Opus-5 harness target | Do not substitute the authoring model or a website answer |
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:712:Model selection happens in the host or website. Beta's score thresholds and run-policy records do not select your authoring model. A model appearing in an old transcript is not proof that your current subscription can access it. Recheck the live account picker and official documentation after upgrades or automatic fallbacks.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:714:**ChatGPT web** is useful for manual ideas and reasoning. It does not automatically gain access to local disk. Mode 4 therefore uses deliberate copy/paste: beta emits a prompt, the user submits it in ChatGPT, and the raw response is returned as data. A paid ChatGPT subscription does not provide API credits.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:728:Open-weight models are an optional expert lane, not a fake “free best model.” They may require substantial CPU/GPU memory, storage, model-serving setup, and careful license review. Before relying on one, test hardware fit, context behavior, structured output, tool calling, multimodal needs, quality on representative beta work, and deterministic evidence capture. A locally runnable model can help with private classification or a second opinion, but no open-weight model is endorsed here as universally best and no subscription above automatically provides its hosting.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:730:One family worth evaluating, not automatically selecting, is **Qwen3-Coder**. Its [official introduction](https://qwenlm.github.io/blog/qwen3-coder/) describes agentic coding and tool-use support. The large 480B-total-parameter variant is not a sensible default assumption for an ordinary laptop. Choose an exact checkpoint/quantization that fits your hardware, inspect its license and required tool-call format, and test it on beta's evidence-sensitive work before relying on it. Open weights, open-source software, free hosting and a paid chat subscription are four different things. Nothing in this handbook installs a local serving stack or changes the required Opus-5 benchmark target.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:732:### Safe fallback prompt
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:738:The cumulative download budget for one task is 1,000,000,000 bytes. This is a hard budget, not a recommended target. Assets must have redistribution permission for the exact bytes used, and required license and attribution notices must survive delivery. A known license label is not by itself proof that a particular copy can be redistributed. `declaration_only` records what someone declared; `--permission-verified` records an explicit verification assertion but is not automated legal certification.
