/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:810:### Harden
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:812:> Use Mode 2 Harden on exact bundle `[PATH]` and task `[TASK_ID]` for goal `[GOAL]`. Hash and preserve the baseline. Separate validity defect, weak difficulty, infrastructure issue, and unsupported complaint. Preserve effective compliant mechanisms and criteria. Propose minimal root-cause changes, legal adversarial fixtures, expected difficulty impact, and before/after observables. Respect the three-total-round bundle budget and do not weaken tests to silence QC.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:816:> Use Mode 12 QC Repair on exact bundle `[PATH]` and exactly one report source `[REPORT PATH OR PASTED TEXT]`. Read every supplied file/folder. Intake and analyze without QC execution, source edits, task execution, or revision. Require pinned producer provenance or exact external attestation. Cover every report section and classify findings as Real, False positive, or Vague. Show Q IDs and wait for my selection. Then require dependency closure, allowed/must-update paths, explicit risk choice for each selected finding, and no silent scope expansion. Apply only after authorization; run post-QC on the real diff; attach fresh output evidence when needed; preserve attempt counters and unmeasured score impact.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:820:> Use Mode 5 Upstream for `[FOLDER OR CHECK REQUEST]`. Read status first; inventory without executing; identify commit/hash, component roots, license and exclusions. Compare generator guidance, Input Bundle QC, and Output Bundle QC separately against the active baseline and curated rules. Produce a source-version impact table, alternatives, migration, validation, difficulty impact, risks, and rollback. Import only as NOT_ACTIVE. Wait for a separate proposal-specific approval before activation or beta file changes. Never commit or push.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:828:> Use Mode `[9 Benchmark|11 Reference Library]` on `[FOLDER]` to answer `[QUESTION]`. Work read-only over source, hash and inventory, deduplicate copies and same-run summaries, stratify model/budget/task/judge/version/date, inspect failing assertion targets, and distinguish observed measurements, pinned rules, interpretations, contradictions and hypotheses. Do not execute archived code, copy answers, activate policy, or claim causality from a small sample.
/Users/mac/Desktop/Terminal Bench/beta-task-generator/BETA-GENERATOR-HANDBOOK.md:832:> Independently review analysis `[ANALYSIS_ID]` against the exact bound context and source bytes. Do not rely on its conclusions. Check coverage, citations, subject/source versions, duplicate evidence, counterexamples, classification, proposed scope, solvability, test/rubric overlap, difficulty claims, and unresolved questions. Return only the exact review JSON schema requested by the controller, and preserve uncertainty rather than inventing fields.
